IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`
IMPORT `cp4-pension-index`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 59 -- THE DISABLED CONTRIBUTOR'S CHILD'S BENEFIT AND THE ORPHAN'S BENEFIT.
--
-- Both benefits (paragraphs 44(1)(e) and (f), piece cp3) are one flat monthly amount that is indexed every
-- year from $113.14 in 1991; 1992 adds $35; a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or
-- university (subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition "dependent child", s 42(1), piece cp3) gets half of the
-- amount under paragraph (1)(c).
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: the Pension Index (s 43, piece cp3), as a list beginning with 1986 (the
-- same series the flat rate benefits of sections 56 and 58 use); whether a dependent child is described in
-- subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition (s 42(1), piece cp3).

§ `Section 59 -- amount of the benefit`

§§ `Section 59(1) -- the basic monthly amount`

-- src:1926 | 59 (1) Except in the case of a dependent child described in subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition dependent child in subsection 42(1), a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit payable to the child of a disabled contributor and an orphan’s benefit payable to the orphan of a contributor, is a basic monthly amount consisting of
-- src:1927 | (a) in the year 1991, one hundred and thirteen dollars and fourteen cents;
-- src:1928 | (b) in the year 1992, the aggregate of
-- src:1929 | (i) one hundred and thirteen dollars and fourteen cents, multiplied by the ratio referred to in subparagraph (c)(ii), and
-- src:1930 | (ii) thirty-five dollars; or
-- src:1931 | (c) in the year 1993 or any subsequent year, an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:1932 | (i) the amount of the benefit that would have been payable for a month in the year preceding that year
-- src:1933 | by
-- src:1934 | (ii) the ratio that the Pension Index for the year in which the benefit commences to be payable bears to the Pension Index for the year preceding that year.
@ref Act s 59(1) (src:1926-1934)
GIVEN `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` EQUALS 1991
            THEN JUST 113.14
        IF `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` EQUALS 1992
            THEN CONSIDER `cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` (JUST 113.14) (`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` 1992 `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`)
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN JUST scaled THEN JUST (scaled PLUS 35)
        IF `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` AT LEAST 1993
            THEN `cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` (`s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` (`the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` MINUS 1) `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`) (`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 59(2) -- a dependent child in part-time attendance`

-- src:1935 | Benefit — part-time student
-- src:1936 | (2) In the case of a dependent child described in subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition dependent child in subsection 42(1), a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit payable to the child of a disabled contributor and an orphan’s benefit payable to the orphan of a contributor, is a basic monthly amount equal to 50% of the amount that would otherwise be calculated under paragraph (1)(c).
@ref Act s 59(2) (src:1936)
GIVEN `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 59(2) — the basic monthly amount for a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university` `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` MEANS
    -- "50% of the amount that would otherwise be calculated under paragraph (1)(c)": paragraph (1)(c) is the
    -- rule for 1993 and later; for an earlier year there is no such amount, and the text gives none.
    IF `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` AT LEAST 1993
    THEN CONSIDER `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (50% TIMES amount)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1925 | Amount of benefit
-- src:1926 | 59 (1) Except in the case of a dependent child described in subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition dependent child in subsection 42(1), a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit payable to the child of a disabled contributor and an orphan’s benefit payable to the orphan of a contributor, is a basic monthly amount consisting of
@ref Act s 59(1), (2) (src:1926)
GIVEN `the child is a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 59 — the basic monthly amount of the benefit for the child` `the child is a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university` `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` MEANS
    -- Subsection (1) opens "Except in the case of a dependent child described in subparagraph (b)(ii)"; subsection (2) is that case.
    IF `the child is a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university`
    THEN `s 59(2) — the basic monthly amount for a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university` `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`
    ELSE `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` `the year in which the benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`
